#N canvas 30 30 1340 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 Cut It -- the entry point on the Mac: open this \, not main.pd \, off-device. u_mother-stub draws the Organelle's front panel and impersonates mother.pd \; its controls bind by send name because graph-on-parent draws no cords. ref/workflow.md, f 94;
#X obj 20 140 u_mother-stub;
#X obj 20 740 u_root 17 1 /tmp 33 49 9002;
#X text 190 744 the patch itself: everything above this line is the Mac shim \, which the device never loads., f 60;
#X text 20 990 The arguments are main.pd's but for 3 \, /tmp because there is no /sdcard \, and 6 \, 9002 because this file and a test run cannot share a UDP port \, so the phone's buttons reach the device and not this. Set the Mac's MIDI inputs and outputs to the device's order \, Launchpad first and nanoKONTROL second (ref/architecture.md \, Creation arguments)., f 94;
#X text 20 880 mother.pd loads main.pd by name \, so u_mother-stub never runs on hardware \, where its s~ and catch~ names would collide with mother's own., f 94;
